index d4f4c49..b2f8903 100644
--- a/docs/task-state.md
+++ b/docs/task-state.md
@@ -86,3 +86,9 @@ Reserve counters before dispatch:
 Batch options apply to each invocation. Group only tasks eligible for the same options. Otherwise use separate batches or single starts. Never edit manifests, erase claims or replace a run to bypass limits. Concurrent callers serialize per PR. Unfinished claims prevent duplicate launches. Immutable outputs identified by content retain original attempts and progress.
 
 Caching never replaces live CI, publication checks, reconciliation or final completion checks. See [the developer reference](capture-performance.md) for capture implementation and benchmark reproduction.
+
+## JSON bookkeeping requests
+
+`request --file REQUEST.json` accepts `{ "version": 1, "operation": "start", "arguments": { "spec": "/private/task.json", "run": "retained" } }`. Operation names and argument keys match the existing CLI (hyphens become underscores). Repeated arguments are arrays; switches are booleans; other values are nonempty strings. Unknown fields, wrong types and missing required arguments block before mutation. Responses use `{version:1, ok:bool, operation, result, error}`; blocked requests exit 2. Existing CLI output is unchanged.
+
+After claiming, `handle --spec SPEC --claim CLAIM --value HANDLE.json` retains `{host:"codex",id:"native-handle"}` on that claim and attempt. A different handle requires explicit recovery. `progress --spec SPEC --claim CLAIM --value PROGRESS.json` appends a nonempty progress object to the claim's retained run. Both verify claim ownership and current inputs. These helpers store evidence only; they never invoke or resume agents, judge findings or authorize publication.
